WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.880
Two senators set a november 25th deadline for meta to account for glasses footage. This is MAG 7 Daily,

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:12.360
episode 38. Amazon's cloud quarter, a nvidia credit talk, and a complaint about google search traffic

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:18.240
come next. Then a counterpoint, a bedrock thread, and the calendar. Ron Wyden and Edward

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:23.840
Markey wrote Mark Zuckerberg after reviewers reportedly watched people undress, use the bathroom,

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:28.880
and have sex in AI glasses footage, including people who never knew the camera was on.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:34.360
Techtime says they want the pre-launch privacy checks, the use of the images, and whether

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:35.740
anyone can delete the data.

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:42.240
Two Swedish outlets via Gizmodo found contract labelers in Kenya had seen sexual clips from

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:47.400
the glasses, and the letter says those contractors described undressing bathrooms and sex.

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:52.840
Metas' own disclosures, as the senators cite them, say imagery run through the glasses'

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:55.840
visual AI may be kept and used to train models.

00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:57.680
Human reviewers included.

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:01.360
Owners can turn off retention of visual data for that training.

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:03.440
Vital law reported from the letter.

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:08.400
The Senator's line is that people filmed without consent have no matching control over

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:09.840
how those images are processed.

00:01:11.022 --> 00:01:13.402
Amazon's quarter is the other large print today.

00:01:13.902 --> 00:01:23.242
Turkey A Today has net sales of $201.9 billion, up 12% from $180.2 billion, or 13% if you strip

00:01:23.242 --> 00:01:25.302
a $900 million currency hit.

00:01:25.302 --> 00:01:33.242
operating income jumped 61% to $28.1 billion from $17.4 billion and the margin

00:01:33.242 --> 00:01:41.902
hit a record 13.9%. AWS sales rose 39.3% to $46 billion. The fastest pace in

00:01:41.902 --> 00:01:48.182
nearly five years on a $184 billion annualized run rate. Cloud operating income

00:01:48.182 --> 00:01:55.842
rose 56 percent to $17.8 billion from $11.4 billion. North American sales grew 6 percent

00:01:55.842 --> 00:02:03.942
to $112.9 billion. International sales rose 5 percent to $43.1 billion or 8 percent before

00:02:03.942 --> 00:02:12.882
currency. Net income slipped 2 percent to $20.7 billion. $1.89 cents a share from $21.2 billion

00:02:12.882 --> 00:02:19.642
or $1.95. Mostly because last year included a $9.5 billion pre-tax and

00:02:19.642 --> 00:02:26.722
thropic gain. NewsCord says that $1.89 missed a fact-set consensus of $1.97.

00:02:27.322 --> 00:02:33.202
The same roundup puts free cash flow at a deficit of $42.4 billion for the 12 months

00:02:33.202 --> 00:02:39.602
through September against a positive $14.8 billion a year earlier, with cash spent on property and

00:02:39.602 --> 00:02:46.302
equipment up $94.8 billion. Andy Jassy said AWS growth should top 40% in both

00:02:46.302 --> 00:02:52.262
2027 and 2028, that nobody has ever run a trillion dollar revenue business, and that

00:02:52.262 --> 00:02:56.882
Amazon may have two of them within five to 10 years. Fourth quarter sales are

00:02:56.882 --> 00:03:04.262
guided at $240 to $247 billion, growth of 12 to 16%. Fourth quarter operating

00:03:04.262 --> 00:03:12.162
income is guided at $28.5 to $33.5 billion. Against $25 billion a year earlier. Cash capital

00:03:12.162 --> 00:03:20.562
spending for 2026 stays near $220 billion. Jassy also cited $578 billion of contracted backlog,

00:03:21.142 --> 00:03:27.702
and said 2027 capital spending will be meaningfully higher. Geekwire, inside that roundup, has chief

00:03:27.702 --> 00:03:33.562
financial officer Brian Olsavsky saying Amazon Leo satellite costs are weighing on the fourth quarter

00:03:33.562 --> 00:03:40.162
profit forecast. The register says AWS is installing an AI accelerator every 14 seconds.

00:03:41.095 --> 00:03:46.135
Nvidia is discussing credit guarantees for an end-scale data center that anthropic plans

00:03:46.135 --> 00:03:51.635
